4","author":"Wu","year":"2015","journal-title":"Food Chem."}],"container-title":["Journal of Food Composition and Analysis"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0889157518301959?httpAccept=text\/xml","content-type":"text\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0889157518301959?httpAccept=text\/plain","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,7,2]],"date-time":"2019-07-02T14:14:24Z","timestamp":1562076864000},"score":44.70308,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/linkinghub.elsevier.com\/retrieve\/pii\/S0889157518301959"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2019,6]]},"references-count":19,"alternative-id":["S0889157518301959"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jfca.2018.12.003","ISSN":["0889-1575"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0889-1575","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2019,6]]},"assertion":[{"value":"Elsevier","name":"publisher","label":"This article is maintained by"},{"value":"Discussion about stable carbon isotopic composition indicates large presence of maize in Brazilian soy sauces (shoyu)Response to \u201cDiscussion about stable carbon isotopic composition indicates large presence of maize in Brazilian soy sauces (shoyu)\u201d","name":"articletitle","label":"Article Title"},{"value":"Journal of Food Composition and Analysis","name":"journaltitle","label":"Journal Title"},{"value":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jfca.2018.12.003","name":"articlelink","label":"CrossRef DOI link to publisher maintained version"},{"value":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jfca.2018.04.001","name":"associatedlink","label":"CrossRef DOI link to the associated document"},{"value":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jfca.2019.01.020","name":"associatedlink","label":"CrossRef DOI link to the associated document"},{"value":"simple-article","name":"content_type","label":"Content Type"},{"value":"\u00a9 2018 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.","name":"copyright","label":"Copyright"}]},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]],"date-time":"2026-03-14T05:10:22Z","timestamp":1773465022778,"version":"3.50.1"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]]},"group-title":"oral","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>The stable isotopic composition of precipitation at any given site is strongly influenced by global, regional and local factors. Among these, geographic position (latitude, altitude, distance form moisture sources) and climatic conditions (air temperature; precipitation types, patterns and amount; relative humidity) are considered as being the most important. However, mounting evidence points towards larges-scale atmospheric circulation patterns as having a role that offsets and\/or masks some (or most) of these factors. In this paper, we use modern and palaeo data to show that in regions with complex interactions between climatic influences and thus highly variable moisture sources, such patterns are the main controlling factors on the distribution of \u03b418O and \u03b42H in precipitation. Our study area is SE Europe, where interactions between the North Atlantic Oscillation, the Siberian High, the Scandinavian Pattern (and several other, regional patterns) results in advection of moisture from the Atlantic and Arctic Oceans; the Mediterranean, Black and Caspian Seas; and interior Asia, all with distinctive \u03b418O and \u03b42H values, that are strongly imprinted in that of local precipitation. In turn, these are registered by paleoarchives (cave ice, speleothems, tree ring cellulose) resulting in ambiguous signals that can be interpreted as changes in local\/regional climatic conditions, rather than changes in the source of moisture. We discuss how \u03b418O and \u03b42H (and the secondary d-excess parameter) values in precipitation are linked to the varying strength of the main atmospheric circulation patterns and how regional sedimentary archives register them and further, how we can reconstruct past changes in their dynamics.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5194\/egusphere-egu26-19432","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]],"date-time":"2026-03-14T04:23:53Z","timestamp":1773462233000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Large-scale atmospheric circulation patterns control the stable isotopic composition of precipitation in SE Europe"],"prefix":"10.5194","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9506-0070","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Aurel","family":"Per\u015foiu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"3145","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]],"date-time":"2026-03-14T04:40:39Z","timestamp":1773463239000},"score":39.27754,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/meetingorganizer.copernicus.org\/EGU26\/EGU26-19432.html"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5194\/egusphere-egu26-19432","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]]},"subtype":"other"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,5]],"date-time":"2022-04-05T05:54:33Z","timestamp":1649138073104},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2019,2,1]],"date-time":"2019-02-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1548979200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.elsevier.com\/tdm\/userlicense\/1.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Journal of Food Composition and Analysis"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2019,2]]},"DOI":"10.1016\/j.jfca.2019.01.020","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2019,2,5]],"date-time":"2019-02-05T18:42:04Z","timestamp":1549392124000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["WITHDRAWN: Stable carbon isotopic composition indicates large presence of maize in Brazilian soy sauces (shoyu)"],"prefix":"10.1016","author":[{"given":"M.C.","family":"Morais","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"T.A.","family":"Pellegrinetti","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"L.C.","family":"Sturion","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"T.M.S.","family":"Sattolo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"L.A.","family":"Martinelli","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"78","container-title":["Journal of Food Composition and Analysis"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0889157519301413?httpAccept=text\/xml","content-type":"text\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0889157519301413?httpAccept=text\/plain","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,5,1]],"date-time":"2019-05-01T15:12:43Z","timestamp":1556723563000},"score":37.82548,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/linkinghub.elsevier.com\/retrieve\/pii\/S0889157519301413"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2019,2]]},"references-count":0,"alternative-id":["S0889157519301413"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jfca.2019.01.020","ISSN":["0889-1575"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0889-1575","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2019,2]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T21:21:06Z","timestamp":1791321666833,"version":"4.3.1"},"reference-count":17,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2018,7,1]],"date-time":"2018-07-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1530403200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":